    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20768" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hircōsus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		hircus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that smells like a goat</i>, <i>goatish</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc. 3, 3, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens centurionum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					3, 77</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subulcus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 98, 10</span></i>
			; cf.: licet scripti sint inter hircosos, possint tamen inter
			unguentatos placere, Sen. Fragm. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 12,
				2, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 59, 5</span></i>.</div>
